      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T19:01:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**. Uninitialized Memory in String View (`util/focaltech/main.cc`)** In `CheckEcBuildVersion`, the response payload is read into a fixed 64-byte array (`rx`).\n\n* **The Issue:** The `std::string_view` is unconditionally instantiated with a length of `kRxLen - kEcResponseHeaderSize - kEcResponseNullTerminatorSize` (55 bytes). If `rr.value()` (actual bytes received) is less than 64, the `string_view` will contain embedded null characters `\\0` from the zero-initialized array, leading to malformed log outputs and potential matching errors in `std::any_of`.  \n* **Remediation:** Size the `string_view` dynamically based on `rr.value()`.\n\n```c\nsize_t valid_data_len \u003d std::max\u003csize_t\u003e(0, rr.value() - kEcResponseHeaderSize);\nstd::string_view info(\n    reinterpret_cast\u003cconst char*\u003e(rx.data() + kEcResponseHeaderSize),\n    valid_data_len);\n\n```",
